# An else-if CHAIN is one logical level, however long: it is a flat dispatch,
# and the grammar's right-nesting of ifElse is a parse-tree fact, not a
# property of the code. Dispatch (line 13) must NOT fire.
# ReallyNested (line 37) is six ifs deep down the THEN side and MUST still fire
# -- that is what keeps this fix from degenerating into "stop counting ifs".
deep-nesting 37
